    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nAlthough I can see that it might be useful, the amount of flexibility it might require to be passed to the user makes it not a good fit to be built-in.\n\nThis can be implemented manually via custom `show` that adds extmarks with proper visual representation of modified buffers. Something like this (add this after `require('mini.pick').setup()` and use as `:Pick buffers`):\n\n```lua\nMiniPick.registry.buffers = function()\n  local ns_id = vim.api.nvim_create_namespace('pick-buffers')\n  local show = function(buf_id, items_to_show, query)\n    MiniPick.default_show(buf_id, items_to_show, query, { show_icons = true })\n\n    -- Show `[+] ` prefix for items representing modified buffers\n    vim.api.nvim_buf_clear_namespace(buf_id, ns_id, 0, -1)\n    local opts = { virt_text = { { '[+] ', 'Special' } }, virt_text_pos = 'inline' }\n    for i, item in ipairs(items_to_show) do\n      if vim.bo[item.bufnr].modified then vim.api.nvim_buf_set_extmark(buf_id, ns_id, i - 1, 0, opts) end\n    end\n  end\n\n  MiniPick.builtin.buffers(nil, { source = { show = show } })\nend\n```\n\nClosing as not planned.",
            "created_at": "2025-05-20T09:19:05Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1810#issuecomment-2893608513",
